   "explain": {
    "en": {
     "text": "Tense tells when an action happens. There are three: present, past and future. The present tense describes an action happening now, while the speaker is talking. Present-tense verbs can take the prefix «እየ-» and the helping verb «ነው»: «ፋጡማ ምሳዋን እየበላች ነው». With «ነበር» the action is past («እየመጣ ነበር»); «በሚቀጥለው ዓመት ይመረቃል» is future."
    },
    "am": {
